# deepcopy_depth_cap.tkr — the COL-F0d `deep_copy` fixture (crumb 0024). `main.tks` builds a
# 300-node self-referential `Node` chain (`Node.next: Node | null`) — deeper than the `u8::MAX`
# (255) hard cap — and `deep_copy`s the head. Exits 0 only if the call RETURNS the `error` variant
# (caught by `match`), never a `Node` (which would mean a silent truncation or a shared reference
# at the frontier). The compiler holds no `deep_copy` callers, so this path is not
# fixpoint-exercised. Pinned to the C backend: `deep_copy` emits on the C route only.

Feature: deepcopy_depth_cap — deep_copy fails loud past the 255 depth cap

  Scenario: a_300_node_chain_returns_the_error_variant
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
